      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>The famous piyyut, Yigdal, by Daniel ben Judah Dayyan. Yigdal (Hebrew: יִגְדָּל‎; yighdāl, means “Magnify [O Living God]”) is based on the 13 Articles of Faith formulated by Maimonides (1135-1204). Daniel ben Judah spent eight years in improving it, completing the piyyut in 1404. This was not the only metrical presentment of the 13 Articles of Faith; but it has outlived all others, whether in Hebrew or in the vernacular.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_1"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_1409_notes"/>
